{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#14","number":14,"verdict":"approve","approve_probability":0.72,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":false,"checked_not_built":true,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["Addresses a real reliability problem: broken or silent videos get marked approved and can auto-publish. This is a clear, owner-relevant harm that the proposal explains in plain terms.","Evidence has specific path:line citations and contrasts the sports pipeline, which throws on a missing final.mp4 (src/lib/tools/assemble.ts:84). That shows the fix is consistent with existing patterns. However, the code is described and paraphrased rather than quoted, apart from one error string.","It checks that the behavior does not already exist by comparing the orchestrators and the sports pipeline, and it names the exact stages to change.","Scope is small (S–M, 2-3 files, no schema change) and the success check is concrete: with ffmpeg or TTS disabled, the run ends failed or in review with a clear reason. The silent-stub soft-failure part adds some design ambiguity, but it is still a reasonable build."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":8592,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":484,"list_price_usd":0.01626,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:33:38.365Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#15","number":15,"verdict":"approve","approve_probability":0.68,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":false,"checked_not_built":false,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["Clear, owner-relevant problem: a hands-off agent silently stops posting and the owner only notices days later. This matters directly to a content automation product.","Evidence names concrete path:line locations (publish.ts:197-203, truecrime/orchestrator.ts:247) and a specific finding that callers discard the returned reason. However, it paraphrases the code and does not quote it, and two of the line numbers are approximate (~:254, ~:154).","There is no explicit 'checked whether this already exists' section. It doesn't say whether the UI or the Post/AgentRun models already have a field for failure reasons, so the 'not built yet' claim rests only on the discarded return values.","Effort is S–M and the success check is concrete (disconnect YouTube, run an auto agent, see a 'not posted, here's why' message). The scope is small and well bounded, so it is a reasonable one to build."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":8893,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":475,"list_price_usd":0.0098456,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:33:50.576Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#16","number":16,"verdict":"approve","approve_probability":0.55,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":false,"checked_not_built":false,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["The problem is real and easy to understand: runs and videos stuck as \"running\" and \"rendering\" forever after a restart. The owner would probably want this fixed.","The fix is small and clear: mark stale runs failed on startup or in the scheduler tick. The effort estimate of S and the kill-and-restart success check are both concrete.","The evidence is thin. It quotes only `.catch(console.error)` from `run/route.ts:9-12`. The claim about the orchestrators has no `path:line` and no quoted code. It also never says where it looked for existing recovery code, so \"nothing ever reconciles them\" is asserted, not shown.","Using an `updatedAt` age as the stuck signal could wrongly fail long renders that are still running. The proposal doesn't address this, and it makes the S estimate look optimistic."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":14779,"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1169,"list_price_usd":0.0201128,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:33:56.464Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#17","number":17,"verdict":"not-now","approve_probability":0.35,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":false,"checked_not_built":false,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["No quoted code: it names `variation.ts` and `visualSignature.ts` but gives no `path:line` and no quoted lines, which the standard requires.","It claims the gate is wired only into True Crime and that Reddit, Sports and History have none. It doesn't say where it looked or what it found, so 'checked it doesn't exist' is unsupported.","The motivation is strong and fits the product: it protects the channel from demonetization, and the external links are dated by context. But the scope is loose. It adds rotating pools of hooks, intros, music and voices, plus optional auto-variation, which is more than 'M' for generalizing one gate.","The success check is clear (10 back-to-back videos get flagged), and the title is plain. Those two items don't outweigh the missing evidence."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":8672,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":439,"list_price_usd":0.010077599999999999,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:33:50.358Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#18","number":18,"verdict":"not-now","approve_probability":0.3,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":false,"checked_not_built":false,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["No quoted `path:line` evidence: it names src/lib/tools/script.ts and analytics.ts but quotes no code and gives no line numbers. The only quotes are from external blogs.","It does not say where it checked that a hook gate or hook scoring doesn't already exist, and it doesn't report what it found. The standard requires this.","The idea is good for the product: a hook gate plus a retention feedback loop ties to the PRD's 'adapt from performance history'. The title, why, effort (M) and success check are all clear.","The scope is bigger than M. It needs candidate generation, scoring, a new table, and a retention correlation that needs ~20 published videos. Sample sizes will be small, so the learning loop is risky to build now."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":8266,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":425,"list_price_usd":0.0094576,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:33:58.628Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#19","number":19,"verdict":"not-now","approve_probability":0.3,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":false,"checked_not_built":false,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["No quoted path:line evidence: it mentions `src/lib/youtube.ts`, `Post` and `PlatformAuth` but quotes no code. The only quoted-style evidence is external blog links, not the repo.","It doesn't show where it checked that TikTok/Instagram support is missing. It just says only youtube.ts is wired, with no search results or file lines.","Effort is L and depends on outside app-review and API onboarding for two platforms. That is a large, risky PR to hand an owner, and the proposal itself says it could be staged.","The title and the 'how we'd know' line are clear. The revenue claims (RPM figures, 4× exposure) come from marketing blogs and are weak justification."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":8707,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":416,"list_price_usd":0.009851599999999999,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:33:59.283Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#20","number":20,"verdict":"not-now","approve_probability":0.35,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":false,"checked_not_built":true,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["The evidence names files and functions (`src/lib/scheduler.ts` `computeNextRun`, `src/lib/tools/publish.ts` `quotaStatus`) but gives no `path:line` and quotes no code. The standard requires quoted lines, so the claims about DST edges and off-by-one risk can't be checked.","The claim that no tests exist rests on one sentence, that tests live only under `src/lib/truecrime/*.test.ts`. It doesn't say how the Scout searched, so the check is thin.","The motivation is sound: silent failures in unattended scheduling and quota code are a real risk, and the plain-English framing is good. Even so, the risk is asserted, not shown with a concrete bug or a quoted suspect line.","It has a clear title, an M estimate and a testable success check (a deliberate off-by-one turns a test red). But it is a general test-coverage proposal, with no demonstrated defect, so the owner may leave it for later."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":10987,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":686,"list_price_usd":0.0121076,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:34:07.452Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#21","number":21,"verdict":"not-now","approve_probability":0.35,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":false,"checked_not_built":false,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["The repo evidence has file paths (`clipIngest.ts`, `visualLint.ts`, `types.ts`) but no `path:line` and no quoted code. The Scout's standard requires both. The only quotes come from outside blog posts.","The claim that there is no license gate anywhere in sports is stated, but the proposal doesn't say where it looked or what it found. It reads as an assertion, not a checked result.","The success check says no sports video can reach `published` with an unlicensed clip. Sports clips come from YouTube broadcast reels, so a fail-closed gate would probably block the whole sports pipeline. The proposal doesn't address this, which undercuts the M estimate.","The problem is real and the title is clear. But the proposal bundles three things: the lint wiring, a new risk-heuristics and checklist system, and an inbox flag. The heuristics part has no defined rules, so it is broader than a single reviewable PR."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":14324,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":905,"list_price_usd":0.0165256,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:34:12.953Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#26","number":26,"verdict":"approve","approve_probability":0.72,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":true,"checked_not_built":true,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["The title and problem are clear to a non-technical owner. The UI promises a spending cap that no code enforces, which is a real trust and money risk.","The evidence quotes the UI text with path:line (`src/app/agents/new/page.tsx:285`, `src/app/settings/page.tsx:197`) and the schema field (`prisma/schema.prisma:39`). That is concrete and specific.","It says where it checked: a repo-wide search of `src/lib` found no reader of `budget` or `monthly_budget`. It also notes that per-run cost is already summed in the truecrime orchestrator, so the work is small.","The effort (S–M) and the success check (set a tiny budget and the run stops with a message) are both concrete. The scope is a bit broad because it bundles a per-run stop with a monthly alert, but a UI-text fallback is offered."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":8940,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":460,"list_price_usd":0.0117916,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:34:08.223Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#27","number":27,"verdict":"approve","approve_probability":0.55,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":false,"checked_not_built":true,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["Clear money motivation for a content platform owner: earn before hitting YouTube's monetization threshold, backed by dated external links.","Cites src/lib/tools/publish.ts:103 and script.ts:71 and describes the code, but doesn't quote the lines verbatim, so the 'quoted, not paraphrased' evidence bar isn't fully met.","Checked non-existence via a repo-wide search for affiliate / commentThreads / descriptionTemplate, and found nothing. That is adequate.","Scope is a bit broad (template, pinned comment, link tracking dashboard) for an 'S–M' estimate. Pinned comments also can't be pinned via the API, and the earnings figures are hype. Still, the description template alone is a small, useful slice."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":8206,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":433,"list_price_usd":0.0106136,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:34:15.659Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#30","number":30,"verdict":"approve","approve_probability":0.72,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":true,"checked_not_built":true,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["It closes a real gap in a fix the owner already approved (PR #25). Recovery only sweeps `status: 'rendering'` (`src/lib/recovery.ts:67-70`), while videos start as `queued` and only become `rendering` at the last step. The result is the same 'stuck forever, no error' problem the module was written to stop.","The evidence is concrete. It quotes the `Video.updateMany` line and gives line numbers for where videos are created as `queued` and where they flip to `rendering` in all three orchestrators. Most of those line numbers are cited without a quote, and the `retrying` claim has no line number, so the evidence is a little thin.","The scope is small and safe. It adds `queued` and `retrying` to the existing sweep and reuses the timeout guard so a live video isn't killed. The S estimate is believable and the change stays in one file.","The success check is clear and testable: kill the app before the render step, wait past the timeout, and the video shows as Failed instead of 'Queued'. The plain-language title and explanation suit a non-technical owner."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":13467,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":872,"list_price_usd":0.015863600000000002,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:34:21.691Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#31","number":31,"verdict":"approve","approve_probability":0.68,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":true,"checked_not_built":true,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["Clear, plain-English title and problem: a dead YouTube login still shows green 'Connected' while posts silently fail. This is a real reliability gap that an owner running an auto-publisher would care about.","Evidence quotes src/lib/youtube.ts:107 (`where: { platform: PLATFORM, status: 'active' }`) and describes the only status writer (manual Disconnect). The Settings page and route citations have no line numbers or quotes, so the evidence is somewhat thin.","Checks that nothing else flips the status, and ties the idea to the earlier PR #28/#29 'why didn't a video post' work. The search for an existing fix is implied more than shown.","Effort S–M and a concrete success check (revoke access, trigger a publish, Settings shows reconnect). The scope is small, but the optional health check adds a little creep."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":8425,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":461,"list_price_usd":0.0114296,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:34:21.379Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#35","number":35,"verdict":"approve","approve_probability":0.55,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":false,"checked_not_built":true,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["Clear, owner-relevant idea: videos play over silence even though a musicIntensity curve (0.3 to 0.95) is already computed. This ties directly to the owner's past complaint that videos 'looked the same and looked bad'.","It checks that the feature is not built. The ffmpeg mux maps only `-map 1:a:0`, and the Remotion path renders only `{audioSrc ? <Audio src={audioSrc} /> : null}` at TrueCrime.tsx:105. That is the one properly quoted line.","The other evidence is weak. The musicIntensity claim cites whole files with no line numbers, and assemble.ts is cited as 'around lines 273-277' with no quote. The Submagic and SendShort competitor claims have no dated link.","The M estimate may be optimistic. It needs sourced, licence-safe music tracks and mixing on two render paths, and the proposal doesn't say where the tracks come from. The success check is concrete: hear music under the narration that swells at the peak without drowning the voice."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":14526,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":961,"list_price_usd":0.015533600000000002,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:34:30.185Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#36","number":36,"verdict":"approve","approve_probability":0.72,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":false,"checked_not_built":true,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["It continues a feature the owner already shipped for sports. The quoted line from Updates/2026-07-14-strong-hooks-for-every-video.md names this exact next step, so the owner is likely to want it.","The title and the what-and-why are clear to a non-technical owner. They explain that the first seconds decide whether a Short works, and that true-crime and history currently get no hook scoring.","The check that it isn't built yet is concrete. It says history/script.ts and truecrime/script.ts prompt for a single hook, and that hookScore and hookStyle are never set for those factories. It does not quote those code lines verbatim, and it gives only approximate line numbers (~181-183, ~97-98, ~103-104). That makes the quoted evidence weaker.","It gives an S–M effort estimate and a testable success check: generate one true-crime and one history video, then look for the Hook strength badge in the Review Inbox. Reusing the existing tested scorer keeps the scope small."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":13028,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":846,"list_price_usd":0.0150636,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:34:34.407Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#43","number":43,"verdict":"approve","approve_probability":0.72,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":true,"checked_not_built":true,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["It targets the product's own headline goal. It quotes PRD goal #5 and the Decision guide calling the analytics feedback loop the most important revenue feature, so the owner is likely to want it.","The evidence is concrete. It quotes the calendar rotation `new Date().getDate() % watchlist.length` at `source.ts:68`/`:85` and `caseDiscovery.ts:251`. It also points to the unused `Agent.memory` field at `schema.prisma:40`.","It says where it checked that this doesn't exist. Nothing writes to `Agent.memory`, and analytics are read only by the Winners screen. That shows the gap is real.","The first version is bounded and reuses an existing field. It has an M estimate and a testable success check: post-digest videos beat baseline median views, and memory visibly fills. The risk is scope. Ranking, prompt biasing and a dashboard view together may be closer to L, and the effect of the biasing is hard to verify."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":11023,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":694,"list_price_usd":0.0147116,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:34:32.714Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#45","number":45,"verdict":"approve","approve_probability":0.7,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":true,"checked_not_built":true,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["Addresses a high-stakes risk (defamation from autonomous true-crime posting) that a product owner would care about; the plain-English framing is clear.","Cites a specific line, defamationLint.ts:59, with the code quoted. It shows a concrete hole: partial names such as 'Smith' skip the check and pass.","Checks whether it already exists: it reports that no *.test.ts files exist under src/lib/compliance, and says this was verified.","Includes an M effort estimate and a testable success check ('Smith killed her' is held for review). The scope of matching change, new review trigger and tests is a bit broad, and the external link is only loosely relevant."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":8302,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":398,"list_price_usd":0.0116436,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:34:38.487Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#49","number":49,"verdict":"not-now","approve_probability":0.35,"bar":{"plain_title":false,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":true,"checked_not_built":true,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["This is three projects in one: a full redesign, a tab restructure, and a TikTok bug fix. The proposal itself says the TikTok fix is an S that could be 'pulled out'. Bundling it into an L project delays a real revenue bug and makes the PR hard to review.","The TikTok part is strong. It cites specific lines (`src/lib/tiktok.ts:189`, `:167`, `src/app/api/auth/tiktok/route.ts:6`) and the merged YouTube pattern (`src/lib/youtube.ts:128/165/181`). It shows TikTok has none of this, so the badge stays green while posts fail. It would likely be approved as a standalone S proposal.","The redesign is vague and mostly opinion: 'premium, storybook-beautiful' look, 3 mockup directions, and a tab grouping the proposal says is 'yours to tweak'. The only evidence is the tab list in `hub-nav.tsx`. Phase 0 is mockups, not code, which does not fit a build-on-approval loop, and the redesign has no measurable success check.","The title is long and lists three separate things, so it is not the plain, single-idea title the standard asks for. The success check has three parts, and the first two ('you've picked a design') are subjective."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":14977,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1036,"list_price_usd":0.0196876,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:34:47.692Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#50","number":50,"verdict":"approve","approve_probability":0.68,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":false,"checked_not_built":true,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["Clear plain-English title and a strong why: an autonomous channel factory should learn from performance data without the owner clicking a button.","Small, well-scoped build (S): reuse the existing 60-second tick in instrumentation-node.ts with an hourly throttle, plus a last-refreshed timestamp in the UI.","Checked-not-built is solid: refreshAllMetrics() has only one caller (the manual analytics route), and a repo-wide search found no automatic caller or cron.","Evidence gives path:line references but doesn't quote the code, which misses the 'quoted, not paraphrased' standard. The claims are specific and plausible, so this is a minor gap."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":11143,"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":858,"list_price_usd":0.0178988,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:34:45.550Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#51","number":51,"verdict":"approve","approve_probability":0.56,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":true,"checked_not_built":true,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["Clear, plain-English title and a concrete problem: proper nouns and acronyms are central to all four niches (sports, true crime, history, Reddit), so a voiceover error hurts credibility.","Evidence is grounded in the code: it quotes the `synthesizeNarration(ctx.videoId, ctx.script.narration, ctx.config.voice)` call at `src/lib/history/orchestrator.ts:198`. It also reports a repo-wide search for pronunciation-related terms that found nothing. One shared pre-TTS pass covering every factory is a strong argument.","The two external links carry no dates, which the standard asks for. The proposal never names the TTS engine or confirms it supports SSML or phoneme hints, so feasibility is a little uncertain. The 'fibby for FBI' example is asserted rather than shown.","The effort estimate is M and the success check is testable (a tricky name plus 'FBI' pronounced correctly). The optional Review Inbox flag adds scope that assumes an existing inbox, which slightly weakens the 'M' estimate."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":13273,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":924,"list_price_usd":0.016543600000000002,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:34:51.760Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#56","number":56,"verdict":"approve","approve_probability":0.75,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":false,"checked_not_built":true,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["Clear, real gap: TikTok tokens can expire and the app keeps showing 'Connected', so one of two channels silently stops posting. The owner already merged the equivalent YouTube fix, so they are likely to want parity.","Title is plain English and the what/why is easy for a non-technical owner to follow. The effort (M) is reasonable because a YouTube template exists to copy, and the success check is concrete.","Evidence cites path:line ranges (src/lib/tiktok.ts:177-190, 164-169) but only paraphrases the code. It does not quote it, which misses the 'quoted, not paraphrased' requirement. The YouTube comparison also has no line numbers.","It checked what exists by pointing to YouTube's markNeedsReconnect() and the Settings banner, and says TikTok has none of that. It does not explicitly say it searched for a TikTok equivalent, but the claim is specific enough to be credible."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":8946,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":490,"list_price_usd":0.0106156,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:34:54.496Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#57","number":57,"verdict":"approve","approve_probability":0.66,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":false,"checked_not_built":false,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["Clear, owner-relevant problem: a paid voice silently degrades to the free Kokoro voice, hurting brand consistency and wasting subscription money. It ties to the owner's earlier approvals of silent-failure work.","The evidence gives path:line ranges (tts.ts:104-108, 125-129) and describes a bare `return false`, but doesn't quote the code, so it falls short of the 'quoted, not paraphrased' standard.","It doesn't say where the agent checked for existing failure-surfacing or fallback flagging, and it doesn't verify the claim that the fallback video 'is treated as a success'. The 'checked not built' item is unmet.","Effort (S–M) and a concrete success test (set an invalid ElevenLabs key and see a warning) are given. The scope is small and testable, though the 'optionally hold for review' part is loosely defined."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":8602,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":471,"list_price_usd":0.0106176,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:34:56.294Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#58","number":58,"verdict":"not-now","approve_probability":0.42,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":false,"checked_not_built":false,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["The idea is clear and fits a revenue-focused content tool. It reuses an existing per-platform publisher pattern, and the owner may like more posting destinations.","The evidence is paraphrased, not quoted. Only `assemble.ts:59` has a line number, and it is described in words with no code shown. `publish.ts` and `tiktok.ts` are cited with no line numbers.","The proposal never says where it checked that Instagram or Facebook posting doesn't already exist, or what it found. This is only implied by the mention of YouTube and TikTok.","The M estimate looks optimistic. Meta's publishing API usually needs app review, a business account and a publicly hosted video URL, and the proposal doesn't address any of this. That makes it a heavy build with a setup burden on the owner."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":16758,"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1314,"list_price_usd":0.025483400000000003,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:35:08.519Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#70","number":70,"verdict":"approve","approve_probability":0.66,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":false,"checked_not_built":false,"effort_estimate":false,"success_check":true},"reasons":["This is a real, concrete bug tied to the core workflow. Safari and iOS need 206 range responses, and the proposal says the media route always returns a full 200. That would block the owner's daily review step on Mac and iPhone.","The title and the why are plain and easy to follow. The success check is specific: open the Review Inbox in Safari and on iPhone, and confirm the preview plays and scrubs.","The evidence gives two path:line citations (route.ts lines 12–19 and inbox-card.tsx:154) but quotes no code. It describes the behaviour instead of quoting it, which falls short of the quoted-evidence requirement.","The effort is given as 'S / M', not a single estimate. The proposal also never says where it checked for existing range support, such as middleware or a different route. It only asserts that the route lacks it."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":11720,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":717,"list_price_usd":0.0116616,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:35:06.218Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#71","number":71,"verdict":"approve","approve_probability":0.6,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":false,"checked_not_built":true,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["Real, concrete risk: duplicate videos and double auto-posts waste limited YouTube quota and can look like spam. An owner running an auto-publishing content platform would care about this.","The title is plain English and the why is clear (generation cost, ~1,600 quota units per extra video, duplicate posts). The success check is testable: two simultaneous ticks produce exactly one run.","The evidence gives specific path:line references and names the three tick sources that can overlap. It mostly paraphrases the code, though. Only 'unconditional' and the 'won't double-run' comment are quoted, and there is no verbatim code block, so it falls short of the quoted-evidence bar.","It shows no existing atomic claim by pointing to the missing `where nextRunAt <= now` guard. It doesn't say what else was searched, but this is enough for a fix scoped at M."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":12237,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":766,"list_price_usd":0.012491599999999999,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:35:08.532Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#72","number":72,"verdict":"approve","approve_probability":0.62,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":true,"checked_not_built":false,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["Ties directly to the owner's own PRD promise (\"which formats and topics are actually earning\"). Cost and views are already tracked, and revenue is the missing piece, so the owner is likely to want it.","The title is plain English and the what and why are clear: earnings per video, profit after cost, and earnings per 1000 views for each factory (true-crime, history, sports).","The evidence cites analytics.ts:76 with the exact metric list, which lacks `estimatedRevenue`, plus the CostLedger schema line and the page.tsx cost display. This is concrete and specific.","It never says where it searched to confirm no revenue tracking exists. It only infers that from one line. It also doesn't mention that the monetary OAuth scope would need re-consent, or that channels not yet monetized will return no revenue data, which could make the M estimate optimistic."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":13306,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":841,"list_price_usd":0.0132056,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:35:19.524Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#73","number":73,"verdict":"not-now","approve_probability":0.4,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":false,"checked_not_built":false,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["The evidence gives path:line references but paraphrases them. For example, it says retry.ts:5 'explicitly says' callbacks must be idempotent, and it quotes no actual code. The orchestrator reference is only '~line 192'.","It never says where it checked that dedupe or idempotency protection doesn't already exist. It only lists `create` calls, and says nothing about existing guards or retry wrappers around them.","The double-charge scenario is speculative. It depends on a 'database is locked' error landing right after a successful paid TTS call, and nothing shows that this has happened or that the retry re-runs the paid call.","The problem is real and matters to the owner, since it concerns money and the budget cap. The effort estimate (M) and the success check (force a retry, expect one cost row per step) are clear. But the 'what to build' is vague: it says 'fix the spend tracker' without naming an approach such as idempotency keys or upserts."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":12019,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":775,"list_price_usd":0.012349599999999999,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:35:20.539Z"}
