{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#90","number":90,"verdict":"not-now","approve_probability":0.25,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":false,"checked_not_built":false,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["Evidence is not quoted from the repo: it names `src/lib/truecrime/script.ts` and `src/lib/tools/script.ts` with no line numbers and no quoted code. The only quote-like material is an external blog claim.","It never says whether prompt caching (cache_control) already exists in the Claude calls. It gives no search result for that, so the 'checked it doesn't exist' requirement is not met.","The claim that the system prompt is large enough to benefit is not backed by anything read in the code. Anthropic caching only applies above a minimum prompt size, and small prompts would see little savings. The '~90% bill cut' headline is oversold, since only the cached input portion gets cheaper.","The 'optionally route simple scripts to a cheaper model' add-on widens the scope and could change output quality, which conflicts with the 'no change to quality' claim. The idea itself, cheap and low risk, is reasonable."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":8824,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":486,"list_price_usd":0.0097036,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:36:05.863Z"}
