{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#103","number":103,"verdict":"not-now","approve_probability":0.25,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":false,"checked_not_built":false,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["The evidence has no quoted code with a path:line. It only names `src/lib/compliance/claims.ts` and `src/lib/history/` and says they exist, so the claim that the pipeline is niche-agnostic is unsupported.","The external links (vidiq, outlierkit) carry no dates. The proposal also never says where it checked that a finance niche or topic seed isn't already there. It only separates itself from proposal #72.","The scope is vague. It says \"a new topic seed plus turning on the existing claims/compliance safeguards\" without saying how the claims module handles finance advice. It also admits finance is \"your money/your life\" content, which is a real risk for an automated pipeline and needs more than an assertion.","The rationale is solid: higher-RPM niches matter, and the title is clear. But the RPM figures are generic web numbers, and this is a business-strategy choice more than a concrete, checked improvement. The M effort and the success check are fine."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":11357,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":673,"list_price_usd":0.0123856,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:36:34.258Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#109","number":109,"verdict":"approve","approve_probability":0.62,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":true,"checked_not_built":true,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["Clear, non-technical title and a concrete gap: sports only calls `gateSportsCopyright` (src/lib/orchestrator.ts:8), while true-crime and history also run `gateVideoScript`. Sports videos can therefore auto-publish with no ad-safety check.","Cites specific path:line evidence with a quoted import and a quoted comment (\"gore is not advertiser-friendly on any topic\"). It also reports a repo-wide search for advertiser/gambling/injury outside compliance that found nothing, which covers the 'checked it doesn't exist' requirement.","Low-risk framing: it reuses an existing tested gate and adds a sports term list, with no new subsystem. Protecting ad revenue is a value an owner running a monetized content platform is likely to want.","Weak spots: the Nov 2025 YouTube gambling-rule claim has no dated link. The effort is given as a range (S–M) rather than one size. The 'limited ads trends toward zero' check is hard to measure. None of these is likely to block approval."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":12938,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":880,"list_price_usd":0.015515600000000001,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:36:36.801Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#110","number":110,"verdict":"not-now","approve_probability":0.25,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":false,"checked_not_built":false,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["The problem is overstated. The proposal says assemble is only *allowed* 30 min (`STAGE_TIMEOUT_MS = { assemble: 30 * 60_000 }`), so the orchestrator would already time out a render at 30 min. The sweeper firing at the same moment kills nothing that could have finished.","The double-spend harm is speculative. It needs a render to run right at the limit and the owner to re-run it. The proposal gives no sign that has happened or is likely.","Evidence is thin. The `recovery.ts:19` and `orchestrator.ts:388` values are quoted, but the `recovery.ts:14-16` comment is only paraphrased. There is also no explicit check that a margin or heartbeat doesn't already exist.","Effort S and the success check are reasonable. But the fix is a marginal robustness tweak for an edge case, not a clear win for the owner."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":17012,"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1486,"list_price_usd":0.0269232,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:36:43.676Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#114","number":114,"verdict":"approve","approve_probability":0.8,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":true,"checked_not_built":true,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["Concrete, verifiable bug: it cites publish.ts lines 262, 331, 120 and 531-533 and quotes the code and the wrong comment at line 118. It traces a clear path from YouTube setting 'published' to the TikTok guard throwing.","It hits a headline feature (auto-publishing to both platforms). The failure is silent and shows a confusing error, so the owner will likely want it fixed.","It checked for existing coverage: no test covers auto mode with two platforms. It also notes that the existing test returns early on review-gating.","The effort is S, the fix options are clear, and the success check is specific: a live TikTok Post plus a new two-platform test. There is no external link, but a bug in this repo doesn't need one."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":8173,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":425,"list_price_usd":0.0108896,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:36:42.431Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#115","number":115,"verdict":"not-now","approve_probability":0.4,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":false,"checked_not_built":true,"effort_estimate":false,"success_check":true},"reasons":["The evidence mostly paraphrases the code. It gives path:line ranges (aiStill.ts:76-79, 41-44, 238-247), but the only quoted text is the prompt shape and `media/<videoId>/ai-NN.jpg`. The key claim that cues collapse into ~15 generic themes is not quoted or cited to a line.","The savings look small: about $0.04 per image. It also adds a new DB table and a cache layer, so the review cost may outweigh the saving.","The claim of 'zero change to the finished videos' is doubtful. AI generation is not deterministic, so reusing a cached image makes visuals repeat across videos where today each run gets a fresh one. The proposal does not address this quality risk.","The effort is given as 'S/M' rather than a single S, M or L. The check for existing caching is good: it compares against the stock-clip `findCachedClip` and the videoId-scoped AI path. The success check is concrete: CostLedger rows drop and a cache-hit counter rises."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":14668,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":940,"list_price_usd":0.016075600000000002,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:36:51.469Z"}
{"id":"alessiopagliarulo/content-generation-platform#118","number":118,"verdict":"approve","approve_probability":0.72,"bar":{"plain_title":true,"what_and_why":true,"quoted_evidence":true,"checked_not_built":true,"effort_estimate":true,"success_check":true},"reasons":["Clear, plain-English title and problem: winners are ranked by views only even though watch percentage is already fetched and stored (analytics.ts:76/85, schema.prisma:193), which is a concrete, real gap.","Evidence cites specific path:line locations, including the ranking line winnerDigest.ts:43 (b.views - a.views), and gives dated external sources for the retention claim, which ties directly to the owner's monetization goal.","Small, self-contained change to an existing feature with no new APIs or cost. Effort is given as S–M, and the success check is testable: a unit test shows a high-views/low-retention video no longer outranks a high-retention one.","Weaknesses: the checked-not-built section is implicit (it shows the field is unused in the winners code, but does not explicitly say where else was searched). The 'retention-aware score' is also left loosely specified, and the effort is a range rather than a single letter."],"model_requested":"sonnet","model_resolved":"claude-sonnet-5","prompt_version":"1","prompt_sha256":"4e41397ab7355e7622330f31dcfe4af366d8e10d2b5176171eca320802ecb3be","duration_ms":8922,"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":482,"list_price_usd":0.012387599999999999,"cli":"2.1.280 (Claude Code)","judged_at":"2026-09-23T18:36:51.356Z"}
